# The shard checks a stamped append against the leaf's entry only, not the
# retired floor. A purge and re-creation of the leaf resets the entry, so an
# activation of the old incarnation, still running, appends into the WAL the
# re-created leaf replays.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsAppendIgnoresRetiredFloor
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
EXPECT: clean (a redundancy check: the guard is implied in the model and kept for the reason in LiveAdvanceDesign.md)
SUMMARY: a stamped append is not refused at or below the retired floor
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the append.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END